@startuml
title Validator Unit Associations
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam roundcorner 0

class "SPU Validator Unit (SPUVU)" as VU <<Component>> {
  + validate(target scope, input)
  + produce SPUValidatorResult
}
class "SPUValidatorResult" as VR <<Class>> {
  validation conclusion
}
class "Validator Unit Association" as VA <<Association>> {
  validatorUnitIdentity
  associationTargetIdentity
  validatorUnitAssociationIdentity
  stepInstanceIdentity
}
class "SPU / Step target scope" as TS <<Entity>> {
  target scope kind
  concrete target instance
}
class "Step Composition" as SC <<Component>> {
  + establishes/maintains associations
  + sole authority for changes/dissociation
}

VU .. VA : participates
VA .. TS : targets exactly one scope
VA .. SC : established by
VU --> VR : produces result
SC .> VU : selects & admits into composition
SC .> TS : target belongs to owning Step

note right of VA : Association = applicability only
Not ownership, not invocation, not result
One VU may have multiple associations to distinct targets

@enduml